# Keyhunt Worker Hosts File
# Format: user@hostname (one per line)
# Lines starting with # are comments
#
# Example entries:
# user@192.168.1.100
# user@192.168.1.101
# root@worker1.example.com
# keyhunt@worker2.local
#
# Note: SSH key authentication must be configured for these hosts
# Run: ssh-copy-id user@hostname

# Local network workers
# user@192.168.1.10
# user@192.168.1.11
# user@192.168.1.12

# Cloud workers
# ubuntu@ec2-xxx.compute.amazonaws.com
# root@vps1.example.com
